---
import Slide from '../ui/Slide.astro';
import Callout from '../ui/Callout.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../ui/CodeBlock.astro';
import Pill from '../ui/Pill.astro';
---

<Slide
  id="s18b-layer-nodes-commands"
  chapter="Layers"
  title="Nodes — Commands"
  notes="Node-first triage: get nodes, describe node for conditions and events, list pods on that node. SSH to kubelet journal if allowed. Myth: NodeNotReady always means dead — often kubelet, CNI, or disk pressure."
>
  <div class="stagger flex flex-col gap-6">
    <section>
      <h3 class="mb-3 font-display text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-deck-cyan">Typical commands</h3>
      <CodeBlock
        lang="bash"
        caption="Node-first triage"
        code={`kubectl get nodes
kubectl describe node <node>   # Conditions, allocatable, events
kubectl get pods -A -o wide --field-selector spec.nodeName=<node>

# On the node (if SSH allowed)
sudo journalctl -u kubelet -n 80 --no-pager`}
      />
    </section>

    <Callout type="myth">
      NodeNotReady always means the node is dead. Often kubelet, CNI agent, or disk pressure — the VM still pings.
    </Callout>

    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 border-t border-deck-border/60 pt-4">
      <Pill tone="amber">Decision hint</Pill>
      <span class="text-lg text-deck-muted">Symptoms on one node only → describe node before describe pod.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</Slide>
